# **What the generated graph needs told**, for `Tools/affected_graph.py`. E2E selection reads, in order:
# `Tools/e2e-affected.map` (file-level, first match decides), then the rules below, then the crate or target that
# owns the path in the generated graph (`Tools/affected-graph.json`); **a path none of them names selects everything**.
# Recorded coverage (`Graph.recorded_coverage`) is what will later replace the map for the paths it names.
#
#   <pattern>   <what>        as in e2e-affected.map, and graph nodes (`crate:<name>`, `target:<name>`, `*` for all):
#                             the sub-stages that reach that node
#   launches <sub-stage pattern> <executable target...>   what a sub-stage starts (Tools/e2e.sh); the first match decides
#   builds   <need> <node...>                             what the catalog's need is built from on the build Mac
#   binary   <binary target> <crate:name>                 what a prebuilt Swift binary target is built from

# The lab (`lab_report`, `run-hostile.sh`); every other sub-stage drives the app, whose bundle carries the service.
launches hostile.production XDictEntryLab
launches hostile.controls   XDictEntryLab
launches hostile.faults     XDictEntryLab
launches hostile.binding    XDictEntryLab
launches reader             XDictEntryLab
launches entries.lab        XDictEntryLab
launches *                  XDict XDictService

# Tools/build-fixtures.sh and Tools/build-lab.sh run xdict-conformance's fixture writers; e2e.sh's sample is
# entries_corpus (a test of xdict-core) and its editions index_bench (an example of it).
builds fixtures crate:xdict-conformance
builds kit      crate:xdict-conformance
builds sample   tests:xdict-core
builds editions tests:xdict-core
binary xdictFFI crate:xdict-ffi

# What the map does not name and no target owns: the package's manifest is the Swift graph itself; resources by the
# target that reads them; the graph's own files.
apps/apple/Package.swift                            all
apps/apple/Resources/DictionaryService*             target:XDictService
apps/apple/Resources/Fonts/*                        target:XDictEntryView
apps/apple/Resources/*                              target:XDict
apps/apple/Strings/*                                target:XDict
